s_id":"geuZssQDB8yblCpFYwoqAw","review_id":"FbOG3EthRHfy1ceOZ7oJ7w","date":"2016-10-29T17:41:10","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9435014128684998,"text_excerpt":"Two of my girlfriends took me here for my birthday dinner last night. It was a couple blocks from my hotel in the French Quarter and had been listed on a \"hottest new restaurants in NOLA\" piece I'd read. We did not regret it. We opted to order the oysters on a half shell and baked oysters to start. They were gulf oysters and both were fantastic. The other standout dishes were the crispy pork belly, the zuchini salad, the blue crab salad in cucumber cups, and the beef tartare. The crawfish beignets were a little salty for me, but they were a favorite of others. For dessert we did the pumpkin chocolate cheesecake, dulce de leche, and bread pudding. All three were phenomenal. This place has ..."},{"business_id":"geuZssQDB8yblCpFYwoqAw","review_id":"IG9cPPDRNEd-OB1U5NXuCQ","date":"2017-02-15T15:15:09","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.942451000213623,"text_excerpt":"What a great dining experience. We arrived a bit early for our reservation and we were seated immediately. Every table in this restaurant has a view of the working kitchen where you can watch food being prepared and the controlled chaos of the evening. The service was as impeccable as the food. First we scoured the wine list and found a unique Vino called \"vending machine double shotgun.\" Apparently this one pays homage to the double shotgun style of architecture of the majority of houses in the New Orleans area. But, it's a California wine just with New Orleans ties. Oh yes, and it's a delicious red blend. I was here with a group of six people who all love to dine together because we thr..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"geuZssQDB8yblCpFYwoqAw","photo_id":"i16GJWPcthmTuniKzeTyBg","label":"drink","image_url":"/photos/i16GJWPcthmTuniKzeTyBg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8929862380027771},{"business_id":"geuZssQDB8yblCpFYwoqAw","photo